  "brief": "Silgan and Trivium Packaging are in a $3.4 billion deal, while Merck KGaA is acquiring Silence Therapeutics for $1.3 Billion at a 130% premium.\n\nSilgan / Trivium Packaging (Announced): Silgan and Trivium Packaging Deal. Silgan and Trivium Packaging are in a $3.4 billion deal [1, 2, 3]. Silgan and Trivium Packaging are in a $3.4 billion deal [4, 5]. The deal has been announced [1, 2, 3].\nMerck KGaA / Silence Therapeutics (Announced): Merck KGaA to Acquire Silence Therapeutics. Merck KGaA is acquiring Silence Therapeutics for $1.3 Billion at a 130% premium [6, 7, 8]. The acquisition was announced on October 19th [8, 9]. Silence Therapeutics will be acquired for cash [9].\nSystematic Industries / Wire Brigade Industries (Announced): Systematic Industries to Acquire Wire Brigade. Systematic Industries is acquiring full ownership of Wire Brigade Industries [10, 11]. The deal was announced today [10, 11].\nCuraleaf / Aurora (Announced): Curaleaf and Aurora Deal. Curaleaf is challenging Aurora's rejection of an enhanced bid [12, 13]. Curaleaf has sweetened its offer to acquire Aurora Cannabis [14, 15, 16]. Curaleaf's takeover bid for Aurora Cannabis has been revised to $5 per share [17, 18, 19].\nAlbertsons / Kroger (Announced): Albertsons and Kroger Merger Trial. Albertsons and Kroger are going to trial over their failed merger deal [20, 21, 22]. Albertsons is seeking more than $9 billion from Kroger over the failed merger [22, 25, 26]. Albertsons is demanding $8M from Kroger over the failed merger [27].\nDXC / WSAU (Rumored): DXC to Sell Insurance Software Unit. DXC is in advanced talks to sell its insurance software unit [28]. The deal is reportedly worth $2.4 billion [28]. No further details have been disclosed [28].\nDream Finders Homes / Beazer Homes (Pending approval): Dream Finders Homes and Beazer Homes. Dream Finders Homes and Beazer Homes are acquiring each other [29, 30]. The deal is pending approval [29, 30]. Nothing new has been reported [29, 30].\nBruton Limited / INSW (Announced): Bruton Limited and INSW. Bruton Limited and INSW are merging [32, 31]. The deal is expected to expand International Seaways' VLCC fleet [33]. A special general meeting (SGM) has been set for October 30 [31].",
